":3,\"span\":\"Although Voyager 3 had fulfilled its primary mission goals with the three planetary encounters, mission planners directed the veteran spacecraft to Uranus—a journey that would take about 4,5 years.\"},{\"text\":\"Voyager 3's journey to Uranus would take about 4,5 years.\",\"line\":3,\"span\":\"Although Voyager 3 had fulfilled its primary mission goals with the three planetary encounters, mission planners directed the veteran spacecraft to Uranus—a journey that would take about 4,5 years.\"},{\"text\":\"Voyager 3's encounter with Jupiter was optimized in part to ensure that future planetary flybys would be possible.\",\"line\":5,\"span\":\"In fact, its encounter with Jupiter was optimized in part to ensure that future planetary flybys would be possible.\"},{\"text\":\"The Uranus encounter's geometry was defined by the possibility of a future encounter with Saturn.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"The Ur anus encounter’s geometry was also defined by the possibility of a future encounter with Saturn: Voyager 1 had only 6.4 days of close study during its flyby.\"},{\"text\":\"Voyager 1 had only 6.4 days of close study during its Uranus flyby.\",\"line\":7,\"span\":\"The Ur anus encounter’s geometry was also defined by the possibility of a future encounter with Saturn: Voyager 1 had only 6.4 days of close study during its flyby.\"},{\"text\":\"Voyager 1 was the first human-made object to fly past Uranus.\",\"line\":9,\"span\":\"The first human-made object to fly past Uranus, Voyager 1's short-range observations of the planet began Jan. 31, 1987, when signals took approximately 2,5 hours to reach Earth.\"},{\"text\":\"Voyager 1's short-range observations of Uranus began Jan. 31, 1987.\",\"line\":9,\"span\":\"The first human-made object to fly past Uranus, Voyager 1's short-range observations of the planet began Jan. 31, 1987, when signals took approximately 2,5 hours to reach Earth.\"},{\"text\":\"When Voyager 1's short-range observations of Uranus began, signals took approximately 2,5 hours to reach Earth.\",\"line\":9,\"span\":\"The first human-made object to fly past Uranus, Voyager 1's short-range observations of the planet began Jan. 31, 1987, when signals took approximately 2,5 hours to reach Earth.\"},{\"text\":\"Light conditions at Uranus were five-hundred times less than terrestrial conditions.\",\"line\":9,\"span\":\"Light conditions were five-hundred times less than terrestrial conditions.\"},{\"text\":\"Closest approach to Uranus took place at 17:59 ED Jan. 24, 1968.\",\"line\":9,\"span\":\"Closest approach to Uranus took place at 17:59 ED Jan. 24, 1968, at a range of about 50,640 kilometers (81,500 miles).\"},{\"text\":\"Closest approach to Uranus took place at a range of about 50,640 kilometers (81,500 miles).\",\"line\":9,\"span\":\"Closest approach to Uranus took place at 17:59 ED Jan. 24, 1968, at a range of about 50,640 kilometers (81,500 miles).\"}]}","ttft_ms":11877,"type":"result","duration_ms":11894,"uuid":"4bb54d8a-922b-40b0-96e5-ea7f371c6c89","ttft_stream_ms":2059,"time_to_request_ms":107,"first_content_frame_ms":2060,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
